---
description: How to use the Virlo MCP tools correctly (pick the right tool, consent before research agents, async jobs, credit awareness)
alwaysApply: true
---

virlo-api-usage:

- For "what works in X" or example videos, start with `find_videos` (instant, $0.05 a page of 25). Use `find_creators` to discover creators. Put every filter in one call; each call draws its own card.
- For the user's own research or data ("my niche", "my agent"), use `ask_virlo` with their words. Earlier work: `list_my_research`.
- `create_research_agent` collects fresh data ($0.50 a run, +$1.00 with Data Intelligence; a recurring agent charges every run). Call it without `user_approved` to get a proposal, explain it and its cost, and set `user_approved: true` only after the user says yes. Write a concrete one-sentence `intent` (goal + niche + content type + exclusions) and 7-12 specific keywords. Do not pass `min_views` or `time_range`.
- Read an agent with `get_agent_report` first, then `get_agent_data` (free): filter by date, platform or views at read time rather than re-running. Instant data reads (trends, sounds, hooks, hashtags, `raw_*`) are billed per call even when empty.
- Paid lookups wait up to ~25 seconds and then return a `job_id` if still running. Research agents usually finish collecting in about 8 minutes (9 in 10 within 20). Tell the user it is running and check once with `check_job_status` on their next message; never poll in a row.
- Treat `finalized: true` as the done signal, not `status === "completed"`: a job can be "completed" with AI analysis still pending. `partial_failure` is still usable data.
- Rank by Virality Score (`sort: most_viral`, or `order_by=weighted_score` / `rising` / `growth` where offered), never raw views, and never compare raw views across platforms.
- Older tool names (`search_keywords`, `create_niche_monitor`, `get_keyword_search_results`, ...) still work for saved scripts but are unlisted. Use the current names.
